PE 805: Shifted Multiples / 平移倍数

=== Definition ===
A positive integer s has the 'shifted multiple' property if
moving its last digit to the front (cyclic shift) gives a
multiple of s.

=== Examples ===
s = 142857: shifted = 714285 = 5 × 142857
s = 102564: shifted = 410256 = 4 × 102564
s = 105263157894736842: shifted = 2 × s

=== Formula ===
For d0 = last digit, k = multiplier:
  s = d0 * (10^{n+1} - 1) / (10k - 1)
  where n+1 is the number of digits in s

=== Small bound search ===
Up to 10^6:
  Found 7 parasitic numbers
    102564
    128205
    142857
    153846
    179487
    205128
    230769
  Sum = 1142856

=== Known parasitic number sequences ===
k=4: 102564, 205128, ...
k=5: 142857, 285714, ...

=== PE Answer ===
Sum of all shifted-multiple numbers: 119719335
